{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent three-stage review of exact commit da43a4e98a2f2bb8effdbab188769c7541c4b060: CHANGES REQUIRED.\n\nStage 1 — Spec Compliance: CONCERN. The certified-plan basis 12a10f3ab4effc1fbad58f47c1dab80e34f07744 is blob-identical to HEAD^ on all three paths, and its three target docstrings are text-identical to the older 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e citations. Normalized executable AST, directive inventory, exact path set, seven-test collection, comment hygiene, diff integrity, trailer validation, and make lint all pass. Full make verify is deferred to CI per operator direction.\n\nStage 2 — Code Quality: FAIL with two IMPORTANT documentation-accuracy findings.\n1. tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/conftest.py:9 describes the only remote as a unique throwaway S3 prefix, but s3_url() returns REBAR_REHEARSAL_S3_REMOTE verbatim when set. State that the prefix may be generated or operator-supplied; teardown still deletes it.\n2. tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/test_cloud_s3_rehearsal.py:7 says Jira-touching scenarios compare issue counts before and after. Only test_inbound_fetch_pulls_both_projects and test_bridge_preview_read_only_and_scoped do; the scoped-fetch and unknown-project scenarios also touch Jira without that count comparison. Name the two scenarios that carry the count oracle.\n\nStage 3 — Domain Integrity: not run because Stage 2 failed. No final three-row receipt was posted.\n\nREVIEW_RESULT: {\"per_stage\":[{\"stage\":\"spec-compliance\",\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"findings\":[]},{\"stage\":\"code-quality\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"IMPORTANT\",\"description\":\"Unique generated S3 prefix is overclaimed when an operator-supplied remote is supported.\",\"file\":\"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/conftest.py\",\"line\":9,\"required_change\":\"Describe generated or operator-supplied S3 prefix behavior and retained teardown.\"},{\"severity\":\"IMPORTANT\",\"description\":\"Before/after issue-count coverage is overclaimed for every Jira-touching scenario.\",\"file\":\"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/test_cloud_s3_rehearsal.py\",\"line\":7,\"required_change\":\"Name only the dual-project fetch and preview scenarios that run the count oracle.\"}]},{\"stage\":\"domain-integrity\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"IMPORTANT\",\"description\":\"Not evaluated because Stage 2 failed.\"}]}],\"overall_verdict\":\"CHANGES_REQUIRED\",\"required_changes_count\":2,\"blocking_findings_count\":2}\n\nReview persistence is on this leaf rather than a new .reviews path because the exact three-path contract forbids another tracked file and AGENTS.md makes the ticket the durable record."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788901086160459001,"uuid":"97093d60-31f4-42b7-88e8-4fd32bd6e044"}